1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * '''Josef Franz Hieronymus von Colloredo-Mannsfeld''' (1813-1895), österreichischer Staatsmann, u.a. Mitglied des verstärkten Reichsrats und des Herrenhauses, 1861–67 Landmarschall des niederösterreichischen Landt
2 CONC ags, 1867 Mitglied des böhmischen Landtags und 1868–69 Präsident des Herrenhauses.
2 CONT * [https://www.google.com/search?q=Joseph+Franz+Hieronymus+von+Colloredo-Mansfeld%2C+1813&ie=utf-8&oe=utf-8&aq=t&rls=org.mozilla:nl:official&client=firefox-a '''Princes of Colloredo and Princes of Mansfeld-Bornstedt''']
2 CONT * Hoyer IV,(1484-1540), Count of Mansfeld-Vorderortische, '''Knight of the Golden Fleece'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT >*    Johann Gebhard von Mansfeld-Vorderortische , (d.1562), Prince-Archbishop of Cologne from 1558.
2 CONT >*    Peter Ernest I,(1517-1604), Prince of Mansfeld-Friedeburg, '''Knight of the Golden Fleece'''.
2 CONT >*    Francis Maximilian,(1639-1692), Count of Mansfeld-Bornstedt, '''Knight of the Golden Fleece'''.
2 CONT >*    Henry Francis,(1646-1715), Prince of Fondi, '''Knight of the Golden Fleece'''.
2 CONT >*    John Baptist III, (1656-1729), Count of Colloredo-Mantua, '''Knight of the Golden Fleece'''.
2 CONT >*    Rudolf Joseph, (1706-1788), Count of Colloredo-Waldsee-Mels, '''Knight of the Golden Fleece'''.Count of Colloredo, '''Knight of the Golden Fleece'''.
2 CONT >*    Franz Gundakar, (1731-1807), Count of Colloredo, '''Knight of the Golden Fleece'''.
2 CONT >*    Franz, (1736-1806), Count of Colloredo, '''Knight of the Golden Fleece'' .
2 CONT >*    Rudolf, (1772-1843), Prince of Colloredo-Mansfeld, '''Knight of the Golden Fleece'''.
2 CONT >*    '''Josef''', (1813-1895), Prince of Colloredo-Mansfeld, '''Knight of the Golden Fleece'''.
2 CONT >*    Hieronymus Joseph Franz de Paula, ( 1732- 1812 ), Count of Colloredo-Waldsee-Mels, Prince-Bishop of Gurk from 1761 and Prince-Archbishop of Salzburg from 1771 until 1803.
2 CONT >*    Anton Theodor, (1729-1811), Count of Colloredo-Waldsee-Mels, Cardinal and Prince-Bishop of Olmütz from 1778.
