1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlo_Pellegrini_(caricaturist)
2 CONT
2 CONT Carlo Pellegrini (25 March 1839 – 22 January 1889), who did much of his work under the pseudonym of Ape, was an Italian-born British artist who served from 1869 to 1889 as a caricaturist for Vanity Fair magazine, a leading journal
2 CONC  of London society. His work for the magazine made his reputation and he became its most influential artist.
