2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Czernin en.wikipedia.org - clan Czernin...] 
2 CONT * House of Czernin - From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT *The Czernin family (Czech: Černínové z Chudenic, German: Czernin von und zu Chudenitz) is one of the oldest and most important noble families originating in Bohemia, present-day Czech Republic.
2 CONT ===History===
2 CONT *The family is descended from the clan of "Drslavici", like several other Bohemian families. The first known bearer of the family name was "Comes" and Camerarius regis (1199–1212) Cernin de Chudenic (11?? - 12??). The name of the 
2 CONC family refers to the town of Chudenice in western Bohemia which was in their possession from the 13th century until 1945.
2 CONT *On 18 May 1607 the Czernin family was elevated to the Reichsfreiherrenstand with the title "Freiherr von Chudenitz" (Baron of Chudenitz, svobodný pán z Chudenic) and on 15 March 1623 to the Reichsgrafenstand with "Reichsgraf von 
2 CONC Chudenitz" (Count of Chudenitz, hrabě z Chudenic).
2 CONT *In 1716, Franz Josef, Count Czernin von und zu Chudenitz received permission from the Emperor to hereditary title "Regierer des Hauses Neuhaus" (Ruler of the House of Hradec).[1]
2 CONT *Today most members of the Czernin family live in the Czech Republic, Austria, and the United Kingdom.
2 CONT ===Legend===
2 CONT *It is said that about 1000 years ago, the King had a conflict with a Bohemian nobleman. He was so angry with him, that he sent his troops into the nobleman's castle. The soldiers murdered the whole family except a baby boy, whom 
2 CONC his nurse had hidden in a kettle in the kitchen. When the soldiers withdrew, people found the little child in the kettle and they praised God for this miracle. They called the boy Czernin which means "The Black" in Czech, because 
2 CONC he was black all over his face after having lain in the kettle. The king was so impressed by the peoples loyalty, that he pardoned the little Czernin. [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Czernin '''read more...''']
